  "id": "agbadza_ewe",
  "name": "Agbadza (Ewe social dance-drumming)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Recreational dance-drumming of the Ewe of south-eastern Ghana and Togo, a slower social form of the old war dance atrikpui, played at funerals and community occasions. The gankogui double bell and axatse rattles carry the timeline, kagan and kidi answer, the sogo leads in drum language, and the group sings call-and-response songs. David Locke and Gideon Foli Alorwoyie published its songs and drum language with recordings.",
  "recipe": "classic modern agbadza, groove Percussion, west African branch. single leader group response. lead call-and-response sogo, kidi, kagan, interlocking timeline keeping gankogui, axatse. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
